From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 16:09:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep unsupported MLO devices independent

QCN9274 HW1.0 uses the legacy WBE.1.0 firmware ABI. No compatible MLO
firmware is available for the supported HW1.0 images, so do not expose
single-chip MLO or join these devices to an inter-device WSI group.
Preserve their local datapath IDs and normal non-MLO operation.

Other PCIe devices without the MLO firmware feature also need separate
hardware groups: assigning partner device IDs before rejecting MLO
selects cookie tables and return-buffer managers the firmware does not
use. Preserve graph-based grouping for MLO-capable PCIe firmware and
AHB split firmware, which has no firmware feature bitmap.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -2114,6 +2114,14 @@
 	if (ath12k_ftm_mode)
 		goto invalid_group;
 
+	/* HW1 uses the legacy WBE.1.0 ABI without supported MLO firmware.
+	 * Other PCIe devices require the firmware MLO feature to share IDs.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW10 ||
+	    (ab->hif.bus == ATH12K_BUS_PCI &&
+	     !ath12k_fw_feature_supported(ab, ATH12K_FW_FEATURE_MLO)))
+		goto invalid_group;
+
 	/* The grouping of multiple devices will be done based on device tree file.
 	 * The platforms that do not have any valid group information would have
 	 * each device to be part of its own invalid group.
@@ -2325,6 +2333,11 @@
 
 	if (ag->num_devices == 1) {
 		ab = ag->ab[0];
+		if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW10) {
+			ag->mlo_capable = false;
+			return;
+		}
+
 		/* QCN9274 firmware uses firmware IE for MLO advertisement */
 		if (ab->fw.fw_features_valid) {
 			ag->mlo_capable =
